{
  "slug": "meeting",
  "name": "Meeting",
  "description": "The meeting lifecycle: Prepare for Meeting, In Meeting, Summary, Done -- driven by the recording lifecycle of the meet42 command-line tool (github.com/Work42-Ai/meet42). meet42 reads the calendar, records and transcribes the meeting, and writes the files this workflow reads; every stage assumes it is installed. If `command -v meet42` prints nothing, ask the user, and with their yes the `meet42-setup` skill installs it.",
  "stages": [
    {
      "name": "Prepare for Meeting",
      "ordinal": 1,
      "is_initial": true,
      "is_terminal": false,
      "entry_prompt": "You're in Prepare for Meeting. This meeting runs on the meet42 command-line tool. (1) Run `command -v meet42`. If it prints nothing (or a meet42 command fails because the tool is missing), ask the user whether they want you to install it (never install it without their yes); if they agree, follow the `meet42-setup` skill to install it and grant its permissions before anything else. (2) Transitions are yours to make: when a system event says In Meeting (or Summary, or Done) is now available, run `work42 transition \"<that stage>\"` immediately, even in the middle of another step. Starting the recording writes meeting/started_at, which makes In Meeting available. (3) Read the event with `meet42 show \"$(work42 storage get meeting/event_id)\" --json` (skip it when meeting/event_id is unset: this is an ad-hoc event). It has the title, time, location, meeting link, organizer, attendees with their replies and the description as `notesHTML`. (4) Look at what else this session can reach: run `work42 widget list` and use any other widget's source that helps you prepare (their skills explain how to read them); do not assume which plugins exist. (5) Build the meeting brief as the `meeting-brief` artifact following the `meet42-brief` skill, with a direct link for every resource it highlights.",
      "entry_gate": null,
      "icon": "tray.and.arrow.down",
      "color_light": "#0284C7",
      "color_dark": "#66C8FF",
      "model": "sonnet",
      "provider": "claude"
    },
    {
      "name": "In Meeting",
      "ordinal": 2,
      "is_initial": false,
      "is_terminal": false,
      "entry_prompt": "The recording started -- you're now In Meeting, running on Sonnet to follow the conversation. meet42 is doing the recording (`meet42 record status` shows it) and writing the live transcript to conversation.jsonl in the recording directory from `work42 storage get meeting/recording_dir`. If a meet42 command fails because the tool is missing or too old, ask the user whether to install or update it, and follow the `meet42-setup` skill only if they agree. Keep concise running notes as the conversation happens and answer what the user asks in chat. Stopping the recording writes meeting/ended_at, which makes Summary available: as soon as a system event says Summary is now available, run `work42 transition \"Summary\"` immediately, even in the middle of another step.",
      "entry_gate": "{\"and\":[{\"namespace\":\"meeting\",\"key\":\"started_at\",\"op\":\"exists\"},{\"namespace\":\"meeting\",\"key\":\"ended_at\",\"op\":\"absent\"}]}",
      "icon": "waveform",
      "color_light": "#6D28D9",
      "color_dark": "#9D6BFF",
      "model": "sonnet",
      "provider": "claude"
    },
    {
      "name": "Summary",
      "ordinal": 3,
      "is_initial": false,
      "is_terminal": false,
      "entry_prompt": "The recording stopped -- you're now in Summary, and this is the most important step: build the best possible summary of the meeting. Read everything it produced. (1) The transcript meet42 wrote: conversation.jsonl in the recording directory from `work42 storage get meeting/recording_dir`. Each line is a JSON object with speaker (\"You\" is the user, \"Speaker N\" or \"Them\" are the other side), text and audioStartSeconds; read all of it before writing. (2) The event: `meet42 show \"$(work42 storage get meeting/event_id)\" --json` (skip it when unset). (3) The brief you built: the `meeting-brief` artifact. Never invent anything that is in none of these; say so plainly when something is unclear or missing. First attribute speakers: for each \"Speaker N\" you can match to an attendee with confidence (they are addressed by name, introduce themselves, or the brief says who owns a topic), write the recording directory's speakers.json as {\"Speaker 1\": {\"name\": \"<attendee name>\", \"email\": \"<attendee email>\"}}; leave out any speaker you are not sure about. A wrong name is worse than none. Then build the summary as the `meeting-summary` artifact following the `meet42-summary` skill (header with attendees, overview, decisions, action items with owner, due date and a link when they map to an issue or PR, open questions, and resources mentioned, each as a direct link), using the attributed names. Finally run `work42 storage set meeting/summary '{\"artifact\":\"meeting-summary\",\"action_items\":N}'` with N the number of action items, and `work42 transition \"Done\"`.",
      "entry_gate": "{\"namespace\": \"meeting\", \"key\": \"ended_at\", \"op\": \"exists\"}",
      "icon": "doc.text",
      "color_light": "#B45309",
      "color_dark": "#FFC766",
      "model": "haiku",
      "provider": "claude"
    },
    {
      "name": "Done",
      "ordinal": 4,
      "is_initial": false,
      "is_terminal": true,
      "entry_prompt": "The recap is written -- this meeting is Done. No further action needed.",
      "entry_gate": "{\"namespace\": \"meeting\", \"key\": \"summary\", \"op\": \"exists\"}",
      "icon": "checkmark.circle.fill",
      "color_light": "#15803D",
      "color_dark": "#4CDB73",
      "model": "sonnet",
      "provider": "claude"
    }
  ],
  "transitions": [
    {
      "from": "Prepare for Meeting",
      "to": "In Meeting",
      "description": "the recording is active (meeting/started_at written and meeting/ended_at absent)"
    },
    {
      "from": "Prepare for Meeting",
      "to": "Summary",
      "description": "the recording finished before the preparation turn transitioned (meeting/ended_at written)"
    },
    {
      "from": "In Meeting",
      "to": "Summary",
      "description": "the recording stopped (meeting/ended_at written)"
    },
    {
      "from": "Summary",
      "to": "Done",
      "description": "the recap is written (meeting/summary written)"
    },
    {
      "from": "In Meeting",
      "to": "Prepare for Meeting",
      "description": "back out to prep (recording reset)"
    },
    {
      "from": "Summary",
      "to": "Prepare for Meeting",
      "description": "back out to prep (recording reset)"
    }
  ],
